<worksheet >
    <title>VS-2 Linearly Independent Sets and Coordinate Systems</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. 
      Complete one problem with progress on the other to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
        <p>Determine whether the set
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
      <mrow>\left\{\begin{bmatrix}1\\4\\-2\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}2\\1\\3\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}-1\\3\\-5\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}5\\0\\1\end{bmatrix}\right\}</mrow>
    </md> is a basis for <m>\mathbb{R}^3</m>. If the set is 
            not a basis, determine if the set is linearly independent 
            or if the set spans <m>\mathbb{R}^3</m>.</p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
        <p>Find the change of coordinates matrix from 
          <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
      <mrow>B=\left\{\begin{bmatrix}1\\-1\\2\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}3\\0\\4\end{bmatrix}, \begin{bmatrix}-2\\1\\5\end{bmatrix}\right\}</mrow>
    </md> to the standard basis for <m>\mathbb{R}^3</m>.</p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>